Attribution
===========

This package implements published physical formulations. The following are reproduced
from, and attributed to:

  H. H. Zargari, S. A. Khajeh Mohammadilar, V. Ziaei Laleh (2025).
  "A long-term and pragmatic numerical simulation of wire arc additively manufactured
   ER70S6 and ER316L thin-wall via finite difference method."
  Progress in Additive Manufacturing 10:11647-11663.
  doi:10.1007/s40964-025-01307-x

  Governing equations (1)-(16), the Sahoo-DebRoy pseudo-binary Fe-S surface tension
  relation, the enthalpy-porosity phase-change formulation, the Darcy mushy-zone drag
  law, the Gaussian arc heat-flux model, and the droplet source model.

  P. Sahoo, T. Debroy, M. J. McNallan (1988). Metall. Trans. B 19:483-491.
  Surface tension of binary metal-surface active solute systems.

  P. Pichler et al. (2020, 2022). J. Mater. Sci. 55:4081-4093;
  Int. J. Thermophys. 43. Thermophysical properties and surface tension of
  NIST SRM 1155a (AISI 316L).

Where the source paper is internally inconsistent or under-specified, the divergence is
documented in docs/MASTER_PLAN.md and the behaviour is configurable rather than silently
inherited.
